            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nI thought about it and the conclusion was that it seems to be too complicated to implement concisely. Plus does not 100% fits [the 'mini.git' scope](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-git.txt#L25-L27). While there are other great alternatives:\r\n-[jesseduffield/lazygit](https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit)\r\n- [\"Conflict\" target](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-bracketed.txt#L244) in 'mini.bracketed' (with [\"x\" as default suffix](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-bracketed.txt#L40)) which allows easier navigation to conflicts in already opened buffers.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
